                                    <h2><span class="shaft"><img id="978-0" src="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/icons/patterns/icon_o.png" width=27 height=27 alt="Omnidirectional" title="Omnidirectional" ><img id="978-1" src="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/icons/patterns/icon_c.png" width=27 height=27 alt="Cardioid" title="Cardioid" ></span>Lewitt Audio LCT 340</h2>
                    
                    <h2 class="sub">                    Detachable-Capsule Pencil Condenser Microphone</h2>
                    <p>The LCT 340 is Lewitt Audio&#8217;s flagship small-diaphragm condenser microphone. It is a transformerless FET design with interchangeable half-inch capsules. Currently, Cardioid and Omni capsules are provided.</p><p>Two switches on the mic body provide a variety of pad and filter options. A backlighted legend indicates the current selection for each.</p><p><a rel="shadowbox" href="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images//mic_extras/lewitt/LCT340-stand.jpg"><img src="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/mic_extras/lewitt/LCT340-stand-sm.jpg" class="thumb shaft" alt="Lewitt Audio LCT-340" width="150" /></a>The 4-way pad attenuates the signal by 0dB, 6dB, 12dB, or 18dB.</p><p>The 4-way high-pass filter can be set to:</p><ul><li>flat/disabled</li><li>-6dB/octave @ 300 Hz</li><li>-6dB/octave @ 150 Hz</li><li>-12dB/octave @ 40 Hz</li></ul><p>The two included capsules use externally-polarized (true condenser) elements measuring 12mm in diameter. They are coupled to a low-noise transformerless amplifier circuit. The published self-noise figure for this microphone, 13dBA, is very low for a small-diaphragm design. </p><p><img src="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/mic_extras/lewitt/DTP40Mts-shockmount.jpg" width="150" alt="Lewitt Audio DTP 40 Mts" class="thumb shaft" />The mic ships with two interchangeable capsules (cardioid and omni) in a foam-lined cardboard box. It includes a rubberized mic clip (Lewitt Audio p/n DTP 40 Mts), foam windscreen (LCT 40 Ws), and leather storage pouch (p/n DTP 40 Lb).</p><p>As of 2012, Lewitt is offering the microphone with only the Cardioid capsule for a reduced price of MSRP $519.<p>Permalink: <a href="//recordinghacks.com/microphones/Lewitt/LCT-340">Lewitt Audio LCT-340</a></p><p>The mic was released in 2010.</p>
